I've  just died a very interesting death. It seems to be a "feature", but I 
can't say I think it is a good one...


I visited a general store. Lots of interesting stuff there, more than I could
afford. So I left the shop and trained my pet. After getting all kinds of
nice stuff I returned to the shop. The shopkeeper was nowhere to be seen
this time. Took one step from the entrance and got:
	It gets angry! It hits! It hits! 
	You die...

All right, why did the shopkeeper zap her wand of invisibility on herself?
Normally monsters start zapping their wands/quaffing potions ONLY when they
are going to attack the player - PEACEFUL monsters are *NOT* supposed to do
this!

For characters without esp/see inv., entering shops which may have invisible
shopkeepers is suicidal.

